From b8f600afd5c7d8fcf6d22225e4e203173a937879 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 05:15:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add SQLite database, migrations, repository, and integrate
 into UI

### Motivation
- Provide a persistent SQLite-backed storage for courses and replace in-memory models with a durable repository and schema.
- Ensure database schema versioning and safe migrations when the app initializes.
- Centralize data access behind a repository API to simplify screens and enable testable storage logic.

### Description
- Add `expo-sqlite` dependency and `DatabaseProvider` which wraps the app with `SQLiteProvider` and runs `migrateDatabase` on init, and wire it into `App.tsx` by wrapping `AppNavigator` with `DatabaseProvider` and `CourseRepositoryProvider`.
- Implement database schema and migrations in `src/database/schema.ts` and `src/database/migrations.ts` which create `courses` and `course_holes` tables and set `PRAGMA` options and `user_version` handling.
- Introduce repository interfaces and SQLite implementation: `CourseRepository`, `CourseRepositoryProvider`, and `SqliteCourseRepository` with methods `save`, `getAll`, `getById`, and `delete` and SQL-backed implementations including ID generation and transactions.
- Refactor models and validation: expand `src/models/Course.ts` types, add `courseValidation.ts` to validate and normalize course drafts, and update `CreateCourseScreen` and `CoursesScreen` to use the repository, include loading/error states, input sanitization, and improved UI styling and accessibility.
- Add a `typecheck` npm script in `package.json` and update `package-lock.json` to include `expo-sqlite` and related deps.

### Testing
- No automated tests were executed as part of this change.
